# openssl: the tests make certificates for a pretend phone.
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               python3,
               openssl
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: flickos-phone
Architecture: all
# openssl: this computer's certificate, made once when it's turned on.
# libnotify-bin: what comes from the phone shows as a notification (--action).
# libglib2.0-bin: gdbus, to close one of those notifications. busctl 257
# can't call CloseNotification (its signature is only a number).
# wl-clipboard: text and the clipboard go to and come from the clipboard.
# xdg-utils: opening a page or file from the phone; xdg-user-dirs: the
# Downloads folder. network-manager: nmcli, to listen only on the networks
# where a phone was paired. openssh-client: ssh-keyscan, to check the
# phone's file-server key, and the ssh the file manager's SFTP backend
# runs. python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-3.0: the file chooser of Send Files to
# Phone, and the Phone window (only those commands use GTK).
Depends: python3,
         openssl,
         libnotify-bin (>= 0.8),
         libglib2.0-bin,
         wl-clipboard,
         xdg-utils,
         xdg-user-dirs,
         network-manager,
         openssh-client,
         python3-gi,
         gir1.2-gtk-3.0,
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: send pages, files and text between a phone and FlickOS
 Share a page, a photo or some text on an Android phone with the KDE
 Connect app, choose this computer, and it arrives here as a notification:
 click it to open the page or the file. The other way, Send to Phone in
 the file manager sends files, and so does the panel button, which also
 sends typed text, the clipboard (a copied web address arrives as a page
 the phone offers to open) or a screenshot. The button also rings the phone when
 it's lost, shows its battery, opens the phone's files and lists what
 came from it. The phone popup shows what the phone plays, with play,
 pause and next (flickos-phone player). Phone in the apps menu (while
 the connection is on) is a window for the same actions and for
 everything a phone has sent.
 .
 It is off until turned on (flickos-phone set enabled yes), and then pairs
 with a phone once (flickos-phone pair). It speaks only the part of KDE
 Connect's protocol that moving things, ringing, the battery,
 browsing the phone's files and the choices below need. The phone's
 notifications can be shown here too, for the apps you allow and never
 while the screen is locked
 (flickos-phone set notifications yes); that is off until turned on.
 The phone's calls can be shown too: who is calling, with Mute, and what
 is playing pauses until the call ends (flickos-phone set calls yes).
 That is off until turned on, and nothing is shown while the screen is
 locked.
 The phone can control what's playing here too, and sees its name and picture
 (flickos-phone set media yes). That is off until turned on, and it
 changes nothing while the screen is locked.
 The phone can run commands named on this computer: it is sent only the
 names (flickos-phone commands add NAME COMMAND). The list is empty
 until one is added, and nothing runs while the screen is locked.
 It listens only on the networks where a phone was paired, and nothing
 runs while it is off.
